Implementation Plan — Phase 5: Complete Wazuh SIEM SOC Security Dashboard
Build a production-grade, enterprise Wazuh SIEM Security Operations Center (SOC) Dashboard in ./dashboard/ using React + Vite, strictly adopting Elastic UI (EUI) & OpenSearch / Wazuh Dashboard design aesthetics, component hierarchy, high data density, and guided analyst workflows.

The dashboard is optimized specifically for high-resolution desktop security workstations and fully integrates all backend capabilities built across Phases 1–4.

🏛️ Wazuh SIEM Core Module Architecture & Features
1. 🖥️ Endpoints & Agent Management Module (/endpoints)
Agent Heartbeat & Health: Displays registered Go eBPF agents (ebpf-agent-node-01), connection status, OS kernel version, agent uptime, and ring buffer stats.
Live Telemetry Stream Barometer: Real-time event throughput graph (events/sec) streaming directly from the Go Agent WebSocket (ws://localhost:8900/ws) & REST API.
Process Lineage Inspector: Tree view of active PIDs, parent processes (ppid), UID/GID, and executable binary paths (/usr/bin/*, /tmp/*).
2. 🚨 Security Events & Threat Monitoring Module (/threats)
Wazuh Alert Classification & Rule Levels:
Level 12 - 15: CRITICAL (#dc2626) — Active Ransomware, Rootkits, Privilege Escalation.
Level 8 - 11: HIGH (#ea580c) — Reverse Shell, Memory Injection, Credential Dumping.
Level 4 - 7: MEDIUM (#d97706) — Suspicious File Writes, Port Scanning.
Level 0 - 3: BENIGN / INFO (#059669) — Normal System Operations.
API-Driven MITRE ATT&CK Framework Mapping:
Dynamic MITRE tactic & technique metadata (tactic, technique_id, technique_name, url) served directly by the backend API (/api/v1/alerts) via the mitre_attack response object.
Zero Frontend Hardcoding: The UI dynamically renders whichever tactic and technique IDs are returned by the backend REST endpoint.
Covers ATT&CK techniques such as T1486 (Data Encrypted for Impact), T1059 (Command & Scripting Interpreter), T1496 (Resource Hijacking), T1068 (Exploitation for Privilege Escalation), and T1014 (Rootkit).
Expandable Event Inspector: Clickable log rows expanding to show raw eBPF syscall parameters, 12-dim feature vector scores, and model consensus breakdown (Random Forest vs. XGBoost vs. Isolation Forest).
3. 🛡️ Active Response & Kernel Mitigation Module (/mitigation)
Automated AI Block Engine: Displays real-time automated kernel enforcement actions triggered by the dual-model ML engine (MitigationController).
Manual Analyst Response Control (Interactive):
Manual Block Form: Form to manually block any PID or Destination IP address, with custom timeout (e.g., 5 min, 1 hour, Permanent) and analyst justification notes.
Manual Unblock Control: 1-click [ RELEASE / UNBLOCK ] button calling POST /api/v1/blocks/unblock to flush LSM hooks and BPF map entries.
Kernel LSM & XDP Map Viewer: Live table showing active eBPF map entries (pid_blocklist, ip_blocklist).
4. 🤖 Universal AI Security Analyst Copilot Module (/copilot)
Embedded AI Chat Console: Interactive query drawer connecting directly to /api/v1/copilot/chat (supporting Gemini / OpenAI / Ollama).
Contextual Prompts: Quick action buttons ("Analyze PID 5555", "Summarize Ransomware Detection", "Generate MITRE Containment Playbook").
Incident Report Synthesizer: Formats AI responses into structured SOC Incident Reports with one-click export.
5. 🔍 Wazuh Discover & DuckDB SQL Console Module (/discover)
Live eBPF Syscall Feed: High-density table of all incoming syscall events (SYS_EXEC, SYS_WRITE, SYS_READ, SYS_CONNECT).
DuckDB SQL Workbench: Embedded SQL query editor allowing analysts to execute live analytical queries against telemetry.db via POST /api/v1/telemetry/query.
🎨 Enterprise SIEM Styling & User Navigation
High-Density Desktop Styling (Wazuh EUI Theme)
Palette: #14171d background, #1d212a solid slate panels, #2a303c precision gridlines, #006bb4 active security blue.
Typography: Crisp Inter body text with monospace JetBrains Mono for PIDs, IP addresses, hashes, and raw JSON payloads.
Zero Clutter: No childish gradients, floating glow cards, or unnecessary animations. Pure enterprise security console layout.
Guided Analyst Navigation & Global Search
Universal Top Search Bar: Global search bar queryable across Endpoints, Alerts, PIDs, IPs, Threat Rules, and MITRE IDs.
Automatic Contextual Navigation:
Clicking any PID inside an alert automatically opens its process lineage.
Clicking any threat alert automatically opens the AI Copilot investigation drawer pre-populated with incident details.
Quick-switch tab bar for instantaneous section switching (Overview, Security Events, Endpoints, Active Response, AI Copilot, Discover SQL).
